IRWB-020-H is complete. `src/tensor/` implements the Tix parser and checker, v6 IR, f32 and f64 evaluators, and checked `inline` and `split-sum` passes. `dist/tensor/index.js` exports exactly `compileTix`, `runTix`, and `optimizeTix`. The six corpus programs are in `corpus/tensor/`; their tests are in `tests/tensor/`.

**Only framework change:** `src/framework/passes/define-pass.ts` now exposes `prepareNativeCandidate`. The synchronous Tix optimizer reuses artifact validation, diffing, correspondence, and write checks without changing the async pass lifecycle. Numerical acceptance stays in tensor code.

On the nine-element witness, serial f32 returned `1` and blocked f32 returned `1.000000238418579`. The exact relation rejected the rewrite; the f64-reference tolerance accepted it. Both valid-IR mutants were rejected numerically.

| Check | Result |
|---|---:|
| `npm run build` | Passed |
| `node --test tests/tensor/*.test.mjs` | 20/20 |
| `node --test tests/framework/*.test.mjs` | 226/226 |
| `node --test tests/typed/{passes,project-meta,strategies,audit,inline}.test.mjs` | 27/27 |

No deviations from the revised design. Acceptance is sampled, not a proof for every input. The worktree is clean; nothing was pushed.

